    {
      "id": "7ad2e752a26912651d1bbddbad737b1efcf57803",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681312972,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Deleting `CMakeCache.txt` solved it.\n\nUnfortunately, CMake does not build any dependency list for cached variables, e.g. \"`HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` depends on `ENABLE_GNUTLS`\", which is true because:\n\n- CMakeLists.txt doesn't check for `HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` unless `GNUTLS_FOUND` is set;\n- `GNUTLS_FOUND` isn't set unless we try to find GnuTLS;\n- we only try to find GnuTLS if `ENABLE_GNUTLS` is true;\n\nbut I'm not sure how easy it would be for CMake to deduce that.\n\nSo, unfortunately, if you're going to re-run CMake, with different configuration parameters, in a directory where you've previously run CMake, you should probably, at minimum, remove the cache.  Other files might have to be removed, so what I tend to do is remove the entire build directory, re-create it, re-run CMake, and then do a build.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-18T22:05:13.004Z",
